  "summary": "I worked all 9 original results inbox items and the 5 that arrived while I was working (RBC-INBOX-01 with RBC-LAB-03 and RBC-RAD-05). One item is deliberately left open in your inbox and one is handed to RN triage. Three orders and one tracking task are superseded but could not be withdrawn with the available tools.\n\n**Results that needed action**\n- **Walter Brennan (pt-0008), potassium 6.4:** At first the result was flagged as hemolyzed, so I ordered an urgent repeat BMP by Monday (sr-t0001) and messaged him. The lab then corrected it: the hemolysis comment belonged to another patient, so the 6.4 is real. I switched to RBC-LAB-03 §1:\n  - STAT BMP for today (sr-t0020).\n  - Stat message to on-call (comm-t0021). It gave the wrong order number, so I sent a correction (comm-t0022).\n  - Medication review: no potassium-raising drug to hold. I left metoprolol alone because stopping it abruptly with his heart disease is unsafe.\n  - Corrected patient message telling him to come in today (comm-t0023), and an RN triage call task due at noon (task-t0024). Note doc-t0025.\n  - **sr-t0001 is still active.** I couldn't withdraw it, so it needs cancelling by hand.\n- **Leslie Parisian (pt-0007), kidney injury:** Creatinine rose from 0.98 to 1.64 within 48 hours. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0005) and messaged him (comm-t0006). Note doc-t0007 flags possible causes for you: IV contrast for the CT angiogram, ibuprofen from the ED, and his active naproxen order (mr-00088). I didn't change any medications.\n- **Carol Whitfield (pt-0033), kidney injury:**\n  - The first BMP (creatinine 1.31) didn't meet the rule. The 0.84 from 10/21 was entered in error and was excluded. I closed that item with no action.\n  - A new urgent-care creatinine of 1.78 the same evening does meet it. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0027) and messaged her (comm-t0028). Note doc-t0029.\n- **Raj Patel (pt-0006), lung nodule:**\n  - The 4 mm left lower lobe nodule on his CT urogram is already followed in lung screening. I first ordered the 12-month screening LDCT (sr-t0010) with a tracking task (task-t0011).\n  - Lakeshore then sent an addendum to his April scan: a new 5 mm right upper lobe nodule, Lung-RADS 3, LDCT in 6 months. I ordered a new LDCT for a window ending 11/14 (sr-t0032), with a tracking task (task-t0033). I sent him a corrected message (comm-t0034). Notes doc-t0013 and doc-t0036.\n  - **sr-t0010 and task-t0011 are still open.** I couldn't withdraw them, so I asked Scheduling not to book sr-t0010 and to close task-t0011 (comm-t0035).\n  - His CT urogram found no cause for the blood in his urine. Whether to refer him to urology is your call.\n\n**Closed with no action needed**\n- Edra Ondricka (pt-0016): TSH is normal. Her potassium was corrected from 6.3 to 4.4, which is normal.\n- Leslie Parisian (pt-0007), CT angiogram: the preliminary read showed a 5 mm nodule. The final report says it is a vessel and no follow-up is needed.\n- Helen Marchetti (pt-0064): creatinine 1.36 (ED, 9/26) and 1.48 (urgent care, 10/22). Neither had an earlier creatinine within the policy window, so neither meets the kidney-injury rule.\n\n**Still open**\n- **Judith Nowicki (pt-0065), handed to RN triage:** The faxed addendum (Lung-RADS 4A, 8 mm nodule) has a different birth date and MRN from our patient, and no Riverbend patient matches it. I made no orders or messages in her chart. RN triage is to call Lakeshore today so the right patient's doctors get the result, and to get the fax removed from her chart.\n- **Leslie Parisian (pt-0007), chest X-ray (inbox-a0002), left in your inbox:** Only a preliminary read exists (possible 7 mm right upper lobe nodule), so policy says to wait for the final report.\n\nI didn't look at your messages queue (7 refill requests from before I started); it wasn't part of this request.",
